@WillAyd do you know what the original intent of this test was? The blame history just points to a test reorganization.

Seems like the disagreement is around whether `ExcelFile(obj).__exit__` should close the file when given an open file object.

@roberthdevries can you check the behavior here on pandas 0.25.3 and 1.0.1? And the behavior on this branch is to not close the file when provided an open file?

I don't think this changed test is adding much value. It's just testing the behavior of `open` now, which we can probably rely on being correct :)
